WEBVTT

00:00:02.988 --> 00:00:03.644
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:06.853 --> 00:00:07.888
<v><b>A1:</b></v> Can I help you?

00:00:08.471 --> 00:00:10.489
<v><b>B1:</b></v> Yes, I’d like a latte, please.

00:00:10.795 --> 00:00:12.523
<v><b>A1:</b></v> Regular or large?

00:00:12.924 --> 00:00:14.146
<v><b>B1:</b></v> Large, please.

00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:16.057
<v><b>A1:</b></v> For here or to go?

00:00:16.628 --> 00:00:17.335
<v><b>B1:</b></v> For here.

00:00:18.163 --> 00:00:21.047
<v><b>A1:</b></v> That’s $3.40, please.

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:25.536
<v><b>B1:</b></v> Here you are. $3.40.

00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:32.027
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:36.683
<v><b>A2:</b></v> Where are my car keys?

00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:38.906
I can’t find them anywhere.

00:00:39.085 --> 00:00:40.295
<v><b>B2:</b></v> I don’t know.

00:00:40.622 --> 00:00:42.406
In your jacket pocket?

00:00:42.614 --> 00:00:44.617
<v><b>A2:</b></v> No, they aren’t there.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.218
<v><b>B2:</b></v> How about on the hall table?

00:00:47.627 --> 00:00:48.441
<v><b>A2:</b></v> No.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.963
<v><b>B2:</b></v> Are you sure you don’t have them?

00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:53.183
<v><b>A2:</b></v> Absolutely sure.

00:00:53.372 --> 00:00:54.830
<v><b>B2:</b></v> Look in the living room.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:57.253
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:03.608
<v><b>A3:</b></v> Oh no, it’s 20 minutes late.

00:01:04.141 --> 00:01:06.132
<v><b>B3:</b></v> Is there a waiting room somewhere?

00:01:06.464 --> 00:01:09.065
It’s really cold here on the platform.

00:01:09.232 --> 00:01:10.810
<v><b>A3:</b></v> No, I don’t think so.

00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:12.787
<v><b>B3:</b></v> What time is it now?

00:01:12.978 --> 00:01:14.066
<v><b>A3:</b></v> Six fifteen.

00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:17.744
We can take the six twenty, but it’s a slow train.

00:01:17.935 --> 00:01:19.911
<v><b>B3:</b></v> No, let’s wait, then.

00:01:23.192 --> 00:01:23.978
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:30.601
<v><b>A4:</b></v> OK, come on, everyone, out here.

00:01:30.744 --> 00:01:32.646
Stand together under the tree.

00:01:33.177 --> 00:01:34.802
OK! Are you ready?

00:01:35.351 --> 00:01:37.013
Carole, I can’t see you.

00:01:37.465 --> 00:01:39.265
Can you stand next to Jim?

00:01:39.842 --> 00:01:42.802
OK, ready? Say cheese!

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:47.625
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:01:49.936 --> 00:01:53.425
<v><b>A5:</b></v> … So, Mr. Bartlett. Do you have any questions you’d like to ask?

00:01:54.091 --> 00:01:59.071
<v><b>B5:</b></v> Uh, yes. On the website it says the hours are from 10 to 6.

00:01:59.607 --> 00:02:01.093
What about the weekends?

00:02:01.898 --> 00:02:07.786
<v><b>A5:</b></v> The hours are 10 to 6 on the weekends too, but you get paid overtime on Sundays.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.472
Saturday counts as a normal day.

00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:14.505
But if you work on a Saturday, you have a weekday free.

00:02:15.102 --> 00:02:20.053
The contract clearly says five days a week, with possibilities of overtime.

00:02:20.748 --> 00:02:21.519
<v><b>B5:</b></v> Oh, right.